{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>And the she-ass saw.</b> But he did not see — for the Holy One, blessed be He, gave the animal permission to see more than a person, since because it has understanding, its mind would be unsettled if it saw the destructive angels." "<b>And his sword drawn in his hand.</b> He said: This wicked one has laid aside his craft, for the weapon of the nations of the world is the sword, and he comes against them with his mouth, which is their craft — so I too will seize his and come against him with his craft. And so its end: ״וְאֵת בִּלְעָם בֶּן בְּעוֹר הָרְגוּ בֶּחָרֶב״ (Numbers 31)."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 22, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:12:14.023717800Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}